1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,248
How do you give every promising account the depth of preparation and follow-through you would give your most important opportunity, without multiplying the work?

2
00:00:07,488 --> 00:00:12,108
EMK Signal, EMK's AI-powered go-to-market platform, is built to do just that.

3
00:00:12,348 --> 00:00:16,138
It works out which accounts to go after, who to speak to, and what to say.

4
00:00:16,138 --> 00:00:18,033
And each reply makes the next one sharper.

5
00:00:18,273 --> 00:00:26,160
It brings together fragmented data from CRMs, inboxes and the team's own leads, and finds prospects like successful customers.

6
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:31,080
It searches relevant third-party databases and the web to enrich company information.

7
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:34,134
Then it prioritises accounts using buying signals.

8
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:44,359
Signal then identifies decision-makers, retrieves contact details and prepares tailored outreach across email, LinkedIn and calls in their language.

9
00:00:44,599 --> 00:00:53,364
For ServiceKey, that could mean an email in Italian to a facilities director, connecting the prospect's expansion with ServiceKey's experience supporting similar sites.

10
00:00:53,364 --> 00:00:55,179
The salesperson reviews and sends.

11
00:00:55,179 --> 00:00:58,414
Follow-ups are queued, and feedback improves future drafts.

12
00:00:58,654 --> 00:01:07,109
For management, the Command Centre shows the funnel, where follow-ups are overdue or accounts have stalled, and activity by salesperson, allowing speedier intervention.

13
00:01:07,349 --> 00:01:15,236
EMK Signal puts the company's collective knowledge behind every salesperson, and gives them more time for what matters most: being in front of customers.

